WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.128 --> 00:00:21.119
"I can't believe you're going to be on TV, Ben," Gaby said on the way home from school.

2
00:00:21.139 --> 00:00:23.040
"You'll be famous!"

3
00:00:24.201 --> 00:00:25.061
Ben frowned.

4
00:00:25.081 --> 00:00:26.862
"I don't want to be famous.

5
00:00:27.482 --> 00:00:30.024
I don't even want to be on Kids' Kitchen Showdown."

6
00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:32.353
After Mr.

7
00:00:32.473 --> 00:00:36.134
Icky had picked Ben to be on the TV show, everyone was excited.

8
00:00:39.756 --> 00:00:41.637
Winnie had given Ben a big hug.

9
00:00:41.657 --> 00:00:42.957
"You'll do great!"

10
00:00:44.578 --> 00:00:48.359
Other monsters patted him on the back and gave him the claws-up sign.

11
00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.101
Some monsters even looked a bit jealous.

12
00:00:53.602 --> 00:00:56.463
Gaby was still talking as she and Ben walked along.

13
00:00:56.483 --> 00:00:58.984
"I didn't even know you liked cooking."

14
00:00:59.976 --> 00:01:01.977
"I hate cooking," Ben said.

15
00:01:01.997 --> 00:01:04.297
"Mr. Icky made a mistake.

16
00:01:04.738 --> 00:01:06.958
I accidentally made something that tastes good.

17
00:01:07.418 --> 00:01:09.159
But that doesn't mean I know what I'm doing."

18
00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:12.600
"You're being silly," Gaby said.

19
00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:15.541
"You obviously have talent and don't realize it."

20
00:01:15.561 --> 00:01:20.502
"Well, I'm not going to win the competition," Ben went on.

21
00:01:20.522 --> 00:01:22.323
"The judges are humans.

22
00:01:22.663 --> 00:01:25.684
They're going to choose a human cook—not a monster."

23
00:01:31.688 --> 00:01:37.091
That evening Ben sat on his back stoop, trying to distract himself from the cooking show.

24
00:01:38.672 --> 00:01:41.754
He made himself think about possible birthday presents for Winnie.

25
00:01:41.774 --> 00:01:44.615
"What do witches like?"

26
00:01:45.135 --> 00:01:46.116
he asked himself.

27
00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:48.717
He thought about Winnie's favorite things.

28
00:01:49.458 --> 00:01:50.538
She loved to fly.

29
00:01:51.619 --> 00:01:52.919
Maybe she'd like a new broom?

30
00:01:55.221 --> 00:01:56.461
Ben pulled out his phone.

31
00:01:58.502 --> 00:02:00.804
He found a website that sold flying brooms.

32
00:02:02.432 --> 00:02:04.333
One broom was shaped like a lightning bolt.

33
00:02:05.434 --> 00:02:07.175
Ben watched a demonstration video.

34
00:02:08.435 --> 00:02:12.217
The broom was so fast, it left a streak of fire across the sky.

35
00:02:12.237 --> 00:02:15.759
"Wow!" Ben said.

36
00:02:15.779 --> 00:02:17.960
"Winnie would love this broom.

37
00:02:18.721 --> 00:02:19.901
How much does it cost?"

38
00:02:20.962 --> 00:02:23.043
He scrolled down the page and found the price.

39
00:02:23.063 --> 00:02:27.385
"Six thousand dollars?"

40
00:02:27.926 --> 00:02:28.686
Ben gulped.

41
00:02:29.847 --> 00:02:31.728
There was no way he could afford that.

42
00:02:33.120 --> 00:02:35.601
He looked at some other flying broom websites.

43
00:02:36.262 --> 00:02:39.524
The cheapest broom Ben saw was still too expensive.

44
00:02:40.124 --> 00:02:43.706
It was five hundred dollars, and it looked like a piece of junk.

45
00:02:45.007 --> 00:02:47.968
Ben's shoulders slumped, and he put his phone away.

46
00:02:49.909 --> 00:02:54.192
As Ben brooded, the hedge that ran down the side of his yard shook slightly.

47
00:02:55.933 --> 00:02:57.734
Something was rustling on the ground.

48
00:03:00.495 --> 00:03:01.516
Ben peered over.

49
00:03:03.276 --> 00:03:03.836
"Who's there?"

50
00:03:04.156 --> 00:03:04.617
he said.

51
00:03:05.477 --> 00:03:06.738
There was no answer.

52
00:03:08.538 --> 00:03:10.299
For a moment the hedge was still.

53
00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:12.480
Then it moved again.

54
00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.902
"Something is in there," Ben thought.

55
00:03:17.862 --> 00:03:19.763
He floated over for a closer look.

56
00:03:22.384 --> 00:03:25.886
He moved some of the leaves out of the way and looked in at the branches.

57
00:03:27.867 --> 00:03:30.388
A pair of glowing eyes stared back at him.

58
00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.181
A chill ran down Ben's spine.

59
00:03:33.201 --> 00:03:35.643
"It's a a kitten!"

60
00:03:35.663 --> 00:03:41.786
Meow! The tiny black kitten leaped out of the hedge and straight toward Ben.

61
00:03:42.527 --> 00:03:43.747
Ben jumped to the side.

62
00:03:44.108 --> 00:03:45.628
The kitten landed on the grass.

63
00:03:46.389 --> 00:03:48.210
It looked up at Ben and hissed.

64
00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:52.212
"Oh, boy," Ben said, glancing around.

65
00:03:53.393 --> 00:03:55.914
A lot of monsters and humans loved cats.

66
00:03:56.815 --> 00:03:58.356
But cats hated ghosts!

67
00:04:00.096 --> 00:04:03.779
Ben ran toward his back door with the kitten chasing him all the way.

68
00:04:03.799 --> 00:04:08.642
"Mom will be furious if this beast gets inside," Ben thought.

69
00:04:09.783 --> 00:04:11.504
He shot across his backyard.

70
00:04:12.504 --> 00:04:16.587
The kitten sprinted behind him, hissing and pouncing at his feet.

71
00:04:17.488 --> 00:04:20.950
Ben floated through his fence and into a neighbor's backyard.

72
00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:22.971
He stopped to catch his breath.

73
00:04:22.991 --> 00:04:26.234
"Whew! I think I lost—" Hiss!

74
00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:29.356
Meow! The kitten was on top of the fence.

75
00:04:30.044 --> 00:04:32.126
It leaped down and fell right through Ben.

76
00:04:32.146 --> 00:04:36.609
"Ahh!" Ben dashed through the neighbor's yard and onto the street.

77
00:04:38.231 --> 00:04:40.232
The kitten was still right behind him.

78
00:04:40.973 --> 00:04:43.735
Ben darted upward, flying over the trees.

79
00:04:44.376 --> 00:04:46.397
Looking down, he saw the kitten.

80
00:04:46.938 --> 00:04:50.501
It was still hissing at him, but at least it couldn't fly.

81
00:04:51.722 --> 00:04:54.244
With a sigh of relief, Ben flew home.

82
00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:05.583
On Wednesday morning Ben was one of the first students to arrive in the cooking classroom.

83
00:05:07.324 --> 00:05:08.104
He saw Mr.

84
00:05:08.204 --> 00:05:10.305
Icky pulling pots from one of the cabinets.

85
00:05:14.668 --> 00:05:15.829
"Um, Mr.

86
00:05:15.929 --> 00:05:17.169
Icky," Ben said.

87
00:05:17.189 --> 00:05:19.230
"Can I talk to you for a second?"

88
00:05:20.071 --> 00:05:21.512
Mr. Icky turned around.

89
00:05:21.532 --> 00:05:25.494
"Ah, Ben, my master monster chef!

90
00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:26.615
What do you need?"

91
00:05:27.435 --> 00:05:28.656
Ben put down his books.

92
00:05:29.980 --> 00:05:32.902
"I don't think I should be on Kids' Kitchen Showdown."

93
00:05:34.163 --> 00:05:36.085
"What?" Mr.

94
00:05:36.205 --> 00:05:37.846
Icky peered closely at Ben.

95
00:05:37.866 --> 00:05:40.528
"I'm not really good at cooking.

96
00:05:41.008 --> 00:05:42.890
I make mistakes all the time.

97
00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:46.673
If my food turns out well, it's totally by accident."

98
00:05:48.174 --> 00:05:49.895
"Nonsense," Mr.

99
00:05:49.995 --> 00:05:50.575
Icky said.

100
00:05:50.595 --> 00:05:53.257
"You have a natural talent, Ben.

101
00:05:53.778 --> 00:05:55.919
And I've already given your name to Mr.

102
00:05:55.939 --> 00:05:59.933
Freaky." By now other students were entering the classroom.

103
00:05:59.953 --> 00:06:03.715
"Good morning, everyone," the teacher called.

104
00:06:03.735 --> 00:06:05.595
"Let's get started."

105
00:06:08.457 --> 00:06:09.057
After Mr.

106
00:06:09.157 --> 00:06:12.678
Icky described the morning's assignment, Mog came over to Ben.

107
00:06:12.698 --> 00:06:16.080
"Hey, Ben," Mog said.

108
00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.881
"I heard you talking to Mr.

109
00:06:18.001 --> 00:06:20.882
Icky. I know how you can get out of doing the show."

110
00:06:20.902 --> 00:06:22.382
"You do?"

111
00:06:22.963 --> 00:06:23.903
Ben was doubtful.

112
00:06:24.623 --> 00:06:28.301
Mog was a good friend, but he didn't usually have smart ideas.

113
00:06:29.404 --> 00:06:30.707
Mog leaned in closer.

114
00:06:30.727 --> 00:06:33.173
"Cook badly today!"
